{"task_id": "HumanEval/40", "solution": "def triples_sum_to_zero(l: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if there are three distinct elements in the list that sum to zero.\n    It uses a sorted two-pointer approach for O(N^2) efficiency after sorting.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(l)\n    if n < 3:\n        return False\n\n    sorted_numbers = sorted(l)\n\n    for i in range(n - 2):\n        # Skip duplicate values for the first pointer to optimize redundant checks.\n        if i > 0 and sorted_numbers[i] == sorted_numbers[i - 1]:\n            continue\n\n        left = i + 1\n        right = n - 1\n\n        while left < right:\n            current_sum = sorted_numbers[i] + sorted_numbers[left] + sorted_numbers[right]\n\n            if current_sum == 0:\n                return True\n            elif current_sum < 0:\n                left += 1\n            else: # current_sum > 0\n                right -= 1\n    return False"}
