{"task_id": "HumanEval/31", "solution": "def is_prime(n):\n    \"\"\"Return true if a given number is prime, and false otherwise.\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be an integer.\")\n\n    if n <= 1:\n        return False\n    if n == 2:\n        return True\n    if n % 2 == 0:\n        return False\n\n    i = 3\n    while i * i <= n:\n        if n % i == 0:\n            return False\n        i += 2\n    return True"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/49", "solution": "def modp(n: int, p: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Return 2^n modulo p using binary exponentiation.\n    This function handles non-negative n and positive p, raising ValueError for invalid inputs.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Exponent 'n' must be a non-negative integer.\")\n    if p <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Modulus 'p' must be a positive integer.\")\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1 % p\n\n    result = 1\n    base = 2 % p\n    exponent = n\n\n    while exponent > 0:\n        if exponent % 2 == 1:\n            result = (result * base) % p\n        base = (base * base) % p\n        exponent //= 2\n    return result"}
