{"task_id": "HumanEval/122", "solution": "def add_elements(arr, k):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of elements with at most two digits from the first k elements of arr.\n    It validates inputs for type and range constraints.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Validate input types as per FR1.\n    if not isinstance(arr, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'arr' must be a list.\")\n    if not isinstance(k, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'k' must be an integer.\")\n\n    # Validate input constraints as per FR2.\n    if not (1 <= len(arr) <= 100):\n        raise ValueError(f\"Length of 'arr' must be between 1 and 100, got {len(arr)}.\")\n    for item in arr:\n        if not isinstance(item, int):\n            raise TypeError(f\"All elements in 'arr' must be integers, found {type(item).__name__}.\")\n    if not (1 <= k <= len(arr)):\n        raise ValueError(f\"Input 'k' must be between 1 and the length of 'arr' ({len(arr)}), got {k}.\")\n\n    total_sum = 0\n    # Iterate through the first k elements to identify and sum qualifying elements (FR3, FR4).\n    for i in range(k):\n        element = arr[i]\n        # An element qualifies if its absolute value is less than 100.\n        if -100 < element < 100:\n            total_sum += element\n\n    return total_sum"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/123", "solution": "def get_odd_collatz(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Given a positive integer n, return a sorted list that has the odd numbers in collatz sequence.\n\n    The Collatz conjecture is a conjecture in mathematics that concerns a sequence defined\n    as follows: start with any positive integer n. Then each term is obtained from the\n    previous term as follows: if the previous term is even, the next term is one half of\n    the previous term. If the previous term is odd, the next term is 3 times the previous\n    term plus 1. The conjecture is that no matter what value of n, the sequence will always reach 1.\n\n    Note:\n        1. Collatz(1) is [1].\n        2. returned list sorted in increasing order.\n\n    For example:\n    get_odd_collatz(5) returns [1, 5] # The collatz sequence for 5 is [5, 16, 8, 4, 2, 1], so the odd numbers are only 1, and 5.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int) or n <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must be a positive integer.\")\n\n    odd_numbers_set = set()\n    current_num = n\n\n    while current_num != 1:\n        if current_num % 2 != 0:\n            odd_numbers_set.add(current_num)\n\n        if current_num % 2 == 0:\n            current_num //= 2\n        else:\n            current_num = (3 * current_num) + 1\n\n    # The number 1 is always odd and the last term in the sequence.\n    odd_numbers_set.add(1)\n\n    return sorted(list(odd_numbers_set))"}
